  "problem": "A bag contains $9$ blue marbles, $5$ red marbles, and $6$ green marbles. A marble is drawn at random and replaced before the next draw. This process is repeated $7$ times. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability of selecting a blue marble exactly $3$ times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}.",
